    "highlights": "- Hover effects on text-content links are implemented using `linear-gradient` backgrounds that create an underline, transitioning to a solid block on hover.\n- Aggressive breakpoint scaling for display typography, where sizes often jump non-linearly (e.g., from 48px on mobile to 38px on tablet, then up to 74px on wide desktop).\n- Widespread use of `text-transform: uppercase` combined with tight letter-spacing for structural elements like eyebrows (H6) and section headers.",
    "insights": [
      "The typographic system is almost entirely built around NB International Web, maintaining a strict modernist and utilitarian aesthetic across the site.",
      "NB International Mono Web is utilized surgically for temporal metadata (e.g., superscript years, release dates), providing a subtle, technical contrast to the primary proportional sans-serif.",
      "Akzidenz-Grotesk Extended is reserved exclusively for high-impact interactions (such as the form submit button), adding an unexpected brutalist edge to an otherwise highly uniform type palette."
    ]
